out the mid-map line so neither base's approach is favored, matching cover spacing and chokepoint placement on each side. Verticality is deliberately minimal here compared to the other lanes — this is the flat, ground-hugging close-combat route — though low climbable rubble mounds or a short collapsed-wall step are acceptable. Everything is weathered tan and rust-orange sandstone, dust-caked and battle-worn, dressed with the abandoned-dig-site language (loose grit, scattered excavation rubble) consistent with the rest of the map.
