    {
        Subregion name: left_lane
        Description: Left lane: a tight, claustrophobic route winding through ruined temple alley walls with low half-cover, designed for close-range duels and a hard chokepoint a third of the way in from each base.
        Plan for this region: This region is the left lane: a single continuous, tight, winding ground-level route running the full 42m east-to-west length of the map along its northern edge, connecting the defender base's northern exit (west) to the attacker base's northern exit (east). It is bounded on its north long side by the towering canyon_wall_north cliff face and on its south long side by the central_mid temple courtyard, so the lane reads as a narrow ruined alley pinched between the cliff and the excavated temple core. Its defining character is claustrophobic close-quarters: the usable walking corridor must be kept narrow (roughly 3 to 5m of clear path) even though the region box is wider, achieved by lining the route with ruined temple masonry — partially collapsed sandstone block walls, toppled lintels, broken doorway frames, and freestanding wall fragments of the buried temple complex — that crowd inward and force the path to bend and dogleg rather than run straight, breaking long sightlines so engagements stay short-range. Distribute frequent low half-cover at chest height (fallen wall sections, rubble piles, scattered carved stone blocks, broken column drums) in a staggered rhythm down the whole run so players moving the lane always have a piece of cover within a step. Establish two designed hard chokepoints, one roughly a third of the way in from each base (near the west third and the east third of the lane's length), where the alley walls squeeze to their tightest gap — a single narrow pinch flanked by tall standing wall fragments — forcing one-at-a-time passage and creating the lane's two key duel points. Between the two chokepoints, near the mid-map line, the route opens into a slightly wider rubble-strewn pocket that forms the lateral handoff to the central_mid courtyard on its south side, leaving a gap or breach in the dividing masonry there so players can rotate between this lane and mid. Keep the two halves of the lane near-mirror-symmetric about the mid-map line so neither base's approach is favored, matching cover spacing and chokepoint placement on each side. Verticality is deliberately minimal here compared to the other lanes — this is the flat, ground-hugging close-combat route — though low climbable rubble mounds or a short collapsed-wall step are acceptable. Everything is weathered tan and rust-orange sandstone, dust-caked and battle-worn, dressed with the abandoned-dig-site language (loose grit, scattered excavation rubble) consistent with the rest of the map.
